scheduler: close the placement client before forking workers

The scheduler manager tests the placement client in the master process,
which leaves keep-alive connections to placement open. oslo.service then
forks the workers, which all inherit the same sockets: concurrent
allocation candidate requests are interleaved on them, the workers read
each other's responses (JSONDecodeError, "Placement API service is not
responding", 180s timeouts) and builds fail with NoValidHost, until the
connections are closed for being idle.

Upstream: not merged yet, bug report pending.

